Error [jet.TypestateMarkerWithoutStates]: `Door` has a `#State` marker but no `state { … }` section
  --> tests/ui/typestate/state_section_shape_diagnostics_are_distinct_5.jet:4:5
    |
  4 |     #State(Ready) open: fn(self) {}
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Markers describe facts owned by the struct; without its declared set the marker cannot be checked or reflected
 Fix: Add one `state { Name, … }` section inside `Door: struct`, or remove the typestate marker
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0159
